02:21.190 --> 02:23.025
It's a tight fit.

02:23.192 --> 02:25.778
There's four of us sleeping in a room for two.

02:25.944 --> 02:28.030
It's small. We can't help it.

02:28.197 --> 02:31.992
It's partly because you guys are so big.

02:32.159 --> 02:33.160
Well...

02:33.327 --> 02:36.747
Either me or Kitahara has to sleep on the floor.

02:36.914 --> 02:38.248
Are you sure?

02:38.415 --> 02:40.751
There's no other way that's physically possible.

02:40.918 --> 02:42.544
Sorry.

02:42.711 --> 02:45.756
Anyway, we'll decide later.

02:45.923 --> 02:48.467
Let's go to the beach first!

02:51.387 --> 02:53.389
You look like you're having fun.

02:53.680 --> 02:55.724
Of course!

02:57.226 --> 02:58.727
You're right. This is nice.

03:00.270 --> 03:03.148
Hey! We're going to the beach out back!

03:03.315 --> 03:04.733
Okay!

03:06.944 --> 03:09.154
Sorry to keep you waiting!

03:09.321 --> 03:11.865
- Hey!
- Hurry!

03:13.075 --> 03:14.660
I'm so happy!

03:14.827 --> 03:17.579
This is a page from my youth!

03:17.746 --> 03:19.331
An important memory

03:19.498 --> 03:22.126
in my heart's photo album!

03:24.336 --> 03:27.005
My album is full of censored images!

03:27.172 --> 03:30.175
No need to worry about others
with the place to ourselves.

03:30.342 --> 03:32.177
You're right!

03:32.344 --> 03:34.471
- Let's go somewhere else.
- Why?

03:34.638 --> 03:38.058
There's no one here!
We can dress however we want!

03:38.350 --> 03:40.769
- We're going somewhere else, right?
- Uh... Okay.

03:40.978 --> 03:42.896
I’m not sure why, but that’s okay.

03:45.107 --> 03:46.775
This spot is nice!

03:46.942 --> 03:48.652
It's just a normal beach.

03:48.819 --> 03:51.405
Well, if you like this spot,
I'm okay with it too.

03:51.572 --> 03:53.949
This looks fun.

03:54.116 --> 03:55.868
I'll go get some drinks.

03:56.034 --> 03:57.286
Oh! Me too!

03:58.287 --> 04:00.038
BEACH EQUIPMENT RENTALS
INQUIRE HERE

04:00.205 --> 04:02.833
They're renting out beach umbrellas.

04:03.000 --> 04:04.668
Let's rent one.

04:04.835 --> 04:06.462
I want somewhere to rest.

04:06.628 --> 04:08.130
If you use our service,

04:08.297 --> 04:10.299
we'll lend you guys an umbrella for free.

04:11.633 --> 04:13.260
Use? What do you mean?

04:13.427 --> 04:15.345
We offer those.

04:19.391 --> 04:21.185
Banana boats?

04:21.768 --> 04:24.354
Why don't you three go ride one?

04:24.521 --> 04:26.106
Uh... I'm fine...

04:26.273 --> 04:28.567
This is our chance! Let's ride one, Kitahara!

04:28.734 --> 04:31.236
- I said, I'm--
- So...

04:31.403 --> 04:35.115
How about deciding where we sleep
using the banana boat?

04:35.282 --> 04:38.744
- Whoever falls off first, loses.
- What?!

04:38.911 --> 04:42.456
Of course, if you're too scared, we don't have to.

04:43.248 --> 04:45.000
You said it first!

04:45.209 --> 04:48.504
Excellent! We're on!

04:48.670 --> 04:50.214
Are you sure about this, Iori?

04:50.380 --> 04:52.090
You might end up in the water.

04:52.257 --> 04:53.425
I'm fine!

04:53.592 --> 04:56.261
They have life vests.
And I have a plan.

04:56.428 --> 04:57.763
A plan?

04:57.930 --> 04:59.181
And...

04:59.348 --> 05:02.726
I can't stay scared of the water forever!

05:03.560 --> 05:05.062
By the way...

05:05.229 --> 05:07.481
Do people fall off these boats sometimes?

05:08.315 --> 05:09.816
It doesn't happen very often.

05:09.983 --> 05:13.779
- Then we won't be able to decide who wins.
- You're right.

05:13.946 --> 05:15.989
Well... I guess that's fine.

05:16.156 --> 05:19.326
Let's enjoy some marine sports.

05:19.493 --> 05:22.996
Okay. Please hold on to the handles tight!

05:29.378 --> 05:30.796
TANNING OIL

05:30.963 --> 05:32.297
You bastard!

05:32.464 --> 05:34.258
You're terrible!

05:34.424 --> 05:37.344
How could you stoop so low?!

05:37.511 --> 05:40.055
You guys both did the same thing.

05:40.222 --> 05:41.557
Here we go!

05:47.479 --> 05:50.816
What's wrong, Kohei? You look so tense!

05:50.983 --> 05:54.820
I could say the same! Did you pee your pants
because you're scared of the water?

05:54.987 --> 05:57.823
Want me to do this with one hand?

05:57.990 --> 06:00.951
- Excellent!
- I'm going to accelerate!

06:01.785 --> 06:02.786
Idiots.

06:05.497 --> 06:08.041
That's so nice! They're enjoying their youth!

06:08.208 --> 06:10.586
AINA'S VIEW

06:10.752 --> 06:13.088
REALITY

06:15.007 --> 06:18.093
I can do this! If I use my feet, I can make it!

06:18.260 --> 06:20.554
But he's doing the same thing...

06:22.764 --> 06:25.601
I have to do something about his feet!

06:25.767 --> 06:28.103
Over there! It's the voice actress Kaya Mizuki!

06:28.270 --> 06:30.105
Over there! It's a porn actress!

06:30.272 --> 06:32.065
What?!

06:32.524 --> 06:33.567
Huh?

06:34.818 --> 06:36.862
- They fell off.
- Oh, dear.

06:37.029 --> 06:38.864
They're so sloppy.

06:39.031 --> 06:41.366
- You coward!
- You're the coward!

06:41.533 --> 06:44.244
- Both of you guys are.
- Hey! Was it fun?

06:44.411 --> 06:46.371
I had fun, but...

06:46.538 --> 06:49.750
That's so nice! I want to enjoy my youth too.

06:51.835 --> 06:53.337
Then do you want to ride too?

06:53.503 --> 06:55.839
Huh? Are you sure?

06:59.551 --> 07:02.346
- We're turning right next.
- Okay.

07:06.058 --> 07:07.893
It's so stable!

07:08.060 --> 07:09.102
What's wrong, Aina?

07:09.269 --> 07:10.854
Did you get water in your eyes?

07:13.398 --> 07:14.983
That was a lot of fun.

07:15.150 --> 07:16.360
I'm so tired.

07:17.027 --> 07:18.654
It's still the first day.

07:18.820 --> 07:20.113
Hey, you two!

07:21.448 --> 07:24.326
The license class starts tomorrow.

07:24.493 --> 07:27.412
Review the booklets
before you go to bed tonight, okay?

07:27.579 --> 07:28.830
Okay.

07:28.997 --> 07:31.416
By the way, what about your bed, guys?

07:31.583 --> 07:33.210
Oh... You're right...

07:33.377 --> 07:35.128
Which one of us was winning?

07:38.256 --> 07:40.425
Kohei won by the height of a wave.

07:40.592 --> 07:42.427
No way!

07:42.594 --> 07:45.055
A wave?! That's a measurement error!

07:45.222 --> 07:47.933
- What's wrong?
- Well... Actually...

07:48.100 --> 07:50.686
I see. There's not enough beds.

07:50.852 --> 07:52.896
That's a big problem.

07:53.438 --> 07:55.816
You guys won't be able to sleep.

07:55.982 --> 07:59.277
It'll be dangerous to do the license class
without enough sleep.

07:59.444 --> 08:01.905
- Then let's do this!
- Huh?

08:12.124 --> 08:14.960
You can stretch out in this room.

08:15.127 --> 08:18.714
You have to get a good night's sleep
for the license class.

08:18.880 --> 08:20.465
Well then... Good night!

08:20.632 --> 08:21.925
Good night!

08:41.319 --> 08:43.739
CAN'T SLEEP AT ALL
LET ME SLEEP IN YOUR ROOM

08:43.905 --> 08:47.242
ARE YOU ASLEEP?
PLEASE HELP

08:55.375 --> 08:56.877
Good morning!

08:57.419 --> 08:59.379
- Hey.
- Good morning!

08:59.880 --> 09:01.214
What's wrong?

09:01.381 --> 09:03.925
Someone sent me some messages last night.

09:04.092 --> 09:06.428
Huh?!

09:06.595 --> 09:09.431
What are you doing?!

09:09.598 --> 09:11.558
Well... I don't think

09:11.725 --> 09:13.935
Iori could do anything to those two.

09:14.102 --> 09:16.605
He might not have gotten enough sleep.

09:16.772 --> 09:19.649
Maybe he'll fail the test.

09:19.816 --> 09:20.942
I can imagine that.

09:21.109 --> 09:23.111
No. It'll be fine.

09:23.278 --> 09:26.656
It won't make a difference how much he sleeps.
He's always stupid.

09:28.408 --> 09:30.952
Why can't any of you guys say something?!

09:31.119 --> 09:32.579
Hey, Iori.

09:32.746 --> 09:34.164
Good morning.

09:34.623 --> 09:35.791
I'm telling you now.

09:35.957 --> 09:39.252
I'm confident I can get a higher score than you.

09:39.586 --> 09:41.421
Idiot! Look who's talking.

09:42.422 --> 09:44.549
You got 17 points on the German test!

09:44.716 --> 09:48.678
You just got 20 points by chance!
Don't get so cocky!

09:49.179 --> 09:50.639
Was 20 a perfect score?

09:50.806 --> 09:52.474
A perfect score was 100.

09:52.641 --> 09:55.519
I'm starting to feel a little worried.

09:55.685 --> 09:57.395
Do you want to test them?

09:57.562 --> 09:59.689
Hey, you two! I have a question for you.

10:00.899 --> 10:04.110
Which method of moving
long distances is less tiring?

10:04.277 --> 10:06.905
A, face-down with your face in the water

10:07.072 --> 10:08.490
or B, face-up?

10:08.657 --> 10:09.908
- B!
- B!

10:10.242 --> 10:11.493
Correct.

10:11.660 --> 10:15.247
How deep can open-water divers dive?

10:15.413 --> 10:17.415
- Eighteen meters!
- Eighteen meters!

10:17.582 --> 10:19.209
These questions are easy.

10:19.668 --> 10:22.712
I have an easy question to ask too.

10:23.171 --> 10:24.422
Dressing rooms are good--

10:24.589 --> 10:25.841
No!

10:26.007 --> 10:28.468
I haven't finished asking the question!

10:28.677 --> 10:32.013
Let's try some hard questions.

10:32.180 --> 10:34.975
At what water temperature
will your hands stop moving?

10:35.934 --> 10:37.227
Well...

10:37.394 --> 10:38.812
It's 18 degrees.

10:40.188 --> 10:41.731
You did it, Iori.

10:41.898 --> 10:44.985
- You must have studied a lot.
- Impossible!

10:45.861 --> 10:48.280
Kohei, you have no idea

10:48.446 --> 10:52.450
how much time I spent
reading that booklet last night.

10:52.617 --> 10:53.910
I see.

10:54.077 --> 10:55.787
It's what they call a lucky strike.

10:55.954 --> 11:00.041
It's because I studied hard
without letting my eyes stray.

11:00.208 --> 11:01.501
You bastard!

11:02.586 --> 11:04.546
At what depth is the safety stop done?

11:04.713 --> 11:06.047
Three to six meters.

11:06.673 --> 11:09.009
- Wow.
- Correct!

11:09.217 --> 11:12.929
Then what is the name of the sharp hook
for cutting fishing line and nets?

11:13.096 --> 11:14.472
A Z knife!

11:15.974 --> 11:17.434
Impressive!

11:17.601 --> 11:19.185
What is this hand signal?

11:19.352 --> 11:20.812
- Boobs.
- Hey, wait!

11:20.979 --> 11:22.564
What did you say all of a sudden?

11:22.731 --> 11:24.482
Uh... I made a mistake.

11:24.649 --> 11:26.318
It's "look this way."

11:27.652 --> 11:30.071
- Then what about this?
- Look at the back of my neck.

11:30.238 --> 11:31.239
No, that's not it.

11:31.406 --> 11:32.073
A. CAN'T CLEAR EAR

11:32.949 --> 11:35.493
Don't look! I have to focus on the booklet!

11:35.660 --> 11:37.913
The booklet! Focus on the booklet!

11:38.079 --> 11:40.916
I can imagine what was going on
when he read that part.

11:41.082 --> 11:43.335
His eyes strayed a lot.

11:43.501 --> 11:44.502
Oh, dear.

11:44.669 --> 11:48.673
I can't believe you weren't able to focus
just because of that.

11:49.299 --> 11:50.300
Huh?!

11:57.515 --> 11:58.850
Good morning.

11:59.017 --> 12:00.852
Good morning.

12:01.019 --> 12:02.103
What do you think?

12:02.270 --> 12:04.356
I didn't look, Lalako-tan!

12:04.522 --> 12:07.609
So you couldn't sleep all night?

12:07.776 --> 12:09.903
Though you don't look very tired.

12:10.070 --> 12:11.947
No. I forced myself to sleep.

12:12.113 --> 12:13.365
How?

12:13.531 --> 12:16.076
I made myself black out.

12:16.242 --> 12:17.619
That's some skill.

12:17.786 --> 12:18.453
DO NOT ATTEMPT

12:18.620 --> 12:19.871
Do you call that sleeping?

12:20.038 --> 12:23.083
Well, anyway, I'm glad there were no problems.

12:23.249 --> 12:24.918
We'll make breakfast.

12:25.085 --> 12:26.628
You guys review the material.

12:26.795 --> 12:28.171
- Okay.
- Okay.

12:31.549 --> 12:33.760
We're taking the test here?

12:33.927 --> 12:36.388
I thought we'd do it somewhere more formal.

12:36.554 --> 12:39.474
The test itself is pretty easy.

12:39.641 --> 12:41.893
Most of the questions have four choices.

12:42.060 --> 12:43.895
Huh? Really?

12:44.062 --> 12:46.189
Then why did we work so hard?

12:46.356 --> 12:47.649
What are you talking about?

12:47.816 --> 12:50.986
Listen. This is knowledge about safety.

12:51.152 --> 12:53.613
Studying for safety is never a waste!

12:54.823 --> 12:56.241
I know how you feel.

12:56.408 --> 12:59.703
You're so different when it comes to diving.

12:59.869 --> 13:01.371
We're starting the test, okay?

13:06.084 --> 13:08.378
- Do you think they're going to be okay?
- Hmm?

13:08.545 --> 13:10.171
Are you worried about Iori?

13:10.338 --> 13:12.007
Well... He'll be okay.

13:12.173 --> 13:13.675
But just now...

13:14.092 --> 13:15.593
Boobs.

13:15.844 --> 13:17.554
They're multiple-choice questions.

13:17.721 --> 13:19.889
He doesn't have to write anything.

13:20.056 --> 13:22.142
If you're worried, why don't you go check?

13:22.767 --> 13:24.561
Well...

13:25.854 --> 13:28.648
Chii-chan's so cute.

13:30.859 --> 13:32.152
BOOBS KITAHARA

13:39.576 --> 13:40.910
Chisa!

13:42.245 --> 13:43.663
What did I do?!

13:47.459 --> 13:49.419
Okay! You all passed!

13:50.879 --> 13:53.131
Why is your face all swollen?

13:53.298 --> 13:55.175
It's because I stayed up all night.

14:00.263 --> 14:02.474
Everyone, what's the initial pressure?

14:02.640 --> 14:03.767
Two hundred.

14:03.933 --> 14:05.935
- Two hundred.
- Two hundred.

14:06.478 --> 14:08.980
Let me know when the pressure reaches 60.

14:09.147 --> 14:12.442
- Okay.
- What happens when it reaches 60?

14:12.609 --> 14:14.444
That's when we ascend.

14:14.694 --> 14:15.945
PRESSURE ADJUST OF BCD

14:16.154 --> 14:17.238
When you press the

14:17.405 --> 14:19.699
power inflator on the BCD,

14:20.450 --> 14:22.702
the air enters the vest, and you'll float up.

14:23.745 --> 14:25.955
When you turn it up and press this button,

14:26.456 --> 14:29.084
the air will go out, and you'll sink.

14:35.590 --> 14:37.217
THE AIR DIDN'T GO OUT COMPLETELY

14:39.344 --> 14:41.262
COULDN'T RESIST THE WEIGHT OF THE TANK

14:46.184 --> 14:48.728
Take off your regulator,

14:48.895 --> 14:52.357
remove the water that got in,
and put it on again.

14:53.942 --> 14:57.112
To remove the water that got in,

14:57.278 --> 14:59.864
you can use your breath,

15:00.031 --> 15:03.284
or use the purge button.

15:03.451 --> 15:04.994
Let go of the regulator,

15:05.578 --> 15:07.622
and then...

15:11.501 --> 15:13.378
Calm down.

15:14.963 --> 15:17.423
Here's my advice.

15:17.590 --> 15:19.634
If you lose your regulator,

15:19.801 --> 15:21.344
lower your right shoulder,

15:21.511 --> 15:24.139
and swing your arm up from below.

15:24.305 --> 15:25.807
Your arm will catch the hose.

15:25.974 --> 15:28.518
Great! I'll use the purge button.

15:39.445 --> 15:40.530
Okay.

15:41.364 --> 15:44.284
We're going to let water into our masks
and get the water out.

15:45.118 --> 15:48.329
If you press the top of your mask
and breathe out from your nose,

15:48.496 --> 15:50.540
the water will be ejected out the bottom.

15:51.291 --> 15:52.292
Okay.

15:54.252 --> 15:55.420
I did it!

16:02.010 --> 16:03.344
What's your pressure?

16:03.511 --> 16:04.679
Eighty.

16:04.846 --> 16:07.098
- Sixty.
- Sixty.

16:07.265 --> 16:08.474
We're going to ascend.

16:08.641 --> 16:09.809
Okay.

16:11.060 --> 16:13.813
The ocean in Okinawa is great!

16:14.564 --> 16:17.275
I wish I could stay underwater forever!

16:17.442 --> 16:20.236
We're also lucky to have such good weather.

16:20.403 --> 16:22.572
Your pressure was only 60.

16:23.865 --> 16:26.534
I started out with only 180!

16:26.701 --> 16:30.079
You said 200 before we started diving!

16:30.246 --> 16:31.331
What’s the commotion?

16:31.497 --> 16:33.875
They're talking about their final pressures.

16:34.042 --> 16:35.710
Their numbers when they ascended?

16:35.877 --> 16:39.047
They fight about everything!

16:40.632 --> 16:43.343
By the way, how much pressure
did you have left?

16:44.427 --> 16:46.596
- One hundred ten.
- The same for me.

16:46.763 --> 16:49.390
- I had 120.
- One hundred thirty.

16:49.557 --> 16:50.934
What about you, Nanaka?

16:51.100 --> 16:52.852
I had the same as Chisa-chan.

16:53.436 --> 16:56.147
- That much?
- It's a difference of a whole decimal!

16:56.314 --> 17:00.151
- You guys could have continued diving.
- Maybe.

17:00.318 --> 17:04.364
Why didn't you have us ascend first
and continue diving?

17:05.698 --> 17:07.200
We can't do that!

17:07.367 --> 17:09.911
Diving is a group activity.

17:10.078 --> 17:12.830
If one person ascends, then everyone ascends.

17:13.581 --> 17:17.418
If we had lots of instructors,
things might have been different, though.

17:17.585 --> 17:19.087
I see.

17:19.254 --> 17:20.505
So that means...

17:20.672 --> 17:23.299
Don't hold us back, you loser!

17:23.466 --> 17:26.386
You think you're better than me?!

17:26.552 --> 17:28.346
- I am better than you!
- We just said

17:28.513 --> 17:31.683
it's a group activity a moment ago,
and they're already fighting.

17:31.849 --> 17:33.559
A group activity...

17:35.603 --> 17:38.690
We can't practice when she's here.

17:38.856 --> 17:41.693
She holds us back.

17:41.859 --> 17:43.695
I'm sorry to ask you this...

17:43.861 --> 17:45.571
Can you stop coming?

17:46.406 --> 17:47.407
Aina?

17:48.825 --> 17:50.326
What?

17:50.493 --> 17:52.954
You were spacing out. Are you okay?

17:53.121 --> 17:55.248
What's wrong? Are you tired already?

17:55.415 --> 17:56.874
Where's your enthusiasm, Cakey?

17:57.041 --> 17:58.960
Stop calling me Cakey!

17:59.127 --> 18:01.671
I'm not tired, and I'm enthusiastic!

18:02.171 --> 18:03.756
That's good.

18:03.923 --> 18:06.718
If you're not feeling well, let us know.

18:06.884 --> 18:09.679
Don't try to push yourself.

18:09.846 --> 18:12.473
It's dangerous to tell lies in the ocean.

18:12.724 --> 18:14.434
Understood!

18:15.310 --> 18:16.644
HOW TO EXCHANGE THE OCTOPUS

18:16.853 --> 18:18.479
If your buddy runs out of air,

18:18.646 --> 18:20.064
give your octopus,

18:20.231 --> 18:23.192
which is a spare regulator, to your buddy.

18:24.444 --> 18:26.529
Share your air with your buddy,

18:26.696 --> 18:29.574
hold on to your buddy tight, and ascend.

18:55.767 --> 18:57.727
The ocean is so beautiful...

18:58.353 --> 19:01.731
I can see why they wish they could stay
underwater forever.

19:05.526 --> 19:06.986
What's your pressure?

19:10.698 --> 19:12.909
- Ninety.
- Eighty.

19:13.076 --> 19:16.287
You guys both still have extra? That means...

19:16.454 --> 19:19.040
We have to stop here because of me...

19:19.207 --> 19:22.710
I was fine even at 60 just now.

19:22.877 --> 19:24.504
Maybe I can keep going a little...

19:31.803 --> 19:34.013
- Sixty.
- Okay.

19:44.690 --> 19:46.025
Hey, Cakey.

19:46.984 --> 19:49.987
- What?
- What do you mean, "What"?

19:50.154 --> 19:52.907
You tried to lie about your pressure just now.

19:53.783 --> 19:55.993
They just told us it's bad to

19:56.160 --> 19:58.079
tell lies in the ocean.

19:58.246 --> 20:01.165
I know you had the lowest pressure, but still...

20:01.332 --> 20:02.792
But--

20:04.293 --> 20:06.587
I didn't want everyone to

20:06.754 --> 20:09.424
have to ascend just because of me.

20:10.508 --> 20:14.011
So you weren't lying just because
you didn't want to lose?

20:14.178 --> 20:17.348
I'd never do that! Uh...

20:17.515 --> 20:20.309
I didn't want to cause trouble for everyone.

20:22.603 --> 20:23.688
What's wrong?

20:23.855 --> 20:28.943
Nothing. You know,
you're not a good judge of character.

20:29.110 --> 20:31.946
What?! You don't make sense.

20:32.113 --> 20:34.365
You're the one who doesn't make sense.

20:34.532 --> 20:36.242
Do you think they'd care

20:36.409 --> 20:38.035
about something like that?

20:38.786 --> 20:42.081
- Excuse me!
- Hey!

20:43.749 --> 20:45.126
That's what she said.

20:45.293 --> 20:46.794
I see.

20:46.961 --> 20:49.005
You were worried about that?

20:49.172 --> 20:51.591
- You know, Aina...
- Yes?

20:52.133 --> 20:55.386
Why do you talk so politely to us?

20:55.553 --> 20:59.140
Huh? It's because you're my seniors.
It's natural.

20:59.307 --> 21:01.601
I see. So for you,

21:01.767 --> 21:05.271
it's natural to show respect to seniors, right?

21:05.438 --> 21:06.606
Is that wrong?

21:06.772 --> 21:08.107
In that case...

21:09.817 --> 21:13.863
Don't you think it's natural
that your seniors would be forgiving?

21:14.322 --> 21:18.117
It's no big deal.
You just used up your air a little quick.

21:18.284 --> 21:19.410
Yeah.

21:19.577 --> 21:21.662
That's only natural.

21:21.829 --> 21:24.874
We'll teach you some tricks.

21:25.374 --> 21:27.877
Just work on getting better next time.

21:28.044 --> 21:29.128
Right!

21:30.296 --> 21:33.007
But don't ever lie like that again.

21:33.174 --> 21:36.010
Especially when it comes to safety.

21:36.177 --> 21:38.930
Honesty is the best policy.

21:39.096 --> 21:40.223
Yeah.

21:41.390 --> 21:43.893
The seniors here are different, right?

21:45.978 --> 21:47.396
Yeah!

21:50.566 --> 21:51.901
But, you know,

21:52.568 --> 21:55.404
if you're worried about what we think,

21:55.571 --> 21:59.283
- it means you haven't opened up to us yet.
- Huh?!

21:59.992 --> 22:01.702
That makes sense.

22:01.869 --> 22:03.704
It's just a swimsuit!

22:03.871 --> 22:05.790
Where?! I'll show you an example!

22:05.957 --> 22:09.085
- This is part of our job too!
- No!

22:09.877 --> 22:11.254
Everything worked out.

22:11.420 --> 22:14.632
Iori, it didn't.

22:14.799 --> 22:16.425
Is there another problem?

22:17.844 --> 22:19.679
At this rate,

22:19.845 --> 22:22.431
you're the only one who's going to fail.

22:27.812 --> 22:29.605
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

22:29.981 --> 22:31.315
Seriously.

22:33.568 --> 22:35.486
Here's your mic, Kitahara.

22:35.695 --> 22:39.865
Me too? All right, let's do this!

22:40.157 --> 22:43.661
- Yeah, sing your heart out.
- You guys seem to be having fun.

22:44.954 --> 22:50.960
A fairytale whispers
In a fake world

22:51.127 --> 22:56.882
Hiding in the complete darkness

22:57.049 --> 23:02.847
I reach for the forbidden fruit
In my last days

23:03.014 --> 23:09.103
Now I know the meaning of the song about hope

23:09.312 --> 23:14.400
A broken gear will never stop again

23:14.567 --> 23:21.991
Even if I were to lose everything
I'd still want you to know

23:22.158 --> 23:28.205
Trapped in the sky so far away
I'm praying with ripped off wings

23:28.414 --> 23:34.045
Because we span together
The vows of arpeggio

23:34.211 --> 23:39.967
If life sparkles only to the beat
Of the resonating stars

23:40.134 --> 23:42.970
I'll sacrifice everything

23:43.137 --> 23:47.725
Till death do us apart

23:47.933 --> 23:49.810
Cheers!

23:54.482 --> 23:57.026
Welcome!

24:02.281 --> 24:05.284
Thanks for going out with me.

24:05.701 --> 24:06.869
No way!

24:07.036 --> 24:08.162
I'm getting wet.

24:08.579 --> 24:09.997
Better take off your clothes.

24:11.290 --> 24:13.376
Okay, I will.

24:13.918 --> 24:15.252
Seriously, what's going on!?

24:15.419 --> 24:16.796
NEXT EPISODE
"YOU HAVE THE WRONG IDEA"
